<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Green Gang</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Qing Bang</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Green Gang was a Chinese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/secret-society">secret society</a> that grew out of the boatmen's brotherhoods of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-canal">Grand Canal</a> and became the dominant criminal organisation of early 20th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanghai">Shanghai</a>. Under bosses such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-jinrong">Huang Jinrong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/du-yuesheng">Du Yuesheng</a> it ran opium, gambling and labour rackets from the French Concession. It allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>'s Nationalists, supplying the men for the 1927 massacre of communists in Shanghai.</p></div>
